/** One slot of the gear panel. Nothing is invented: a pick the data does not have is null, and a gap that cannot be scored is null. */
@Serializable
data class CharacterGearSlot(
    @SerialName("slot") val slot: String,
    /** The item the character wears in the slot, from its newest addon export. Null when the slot is empty in the export. */
    @SerialName("worn") val worn: CharacterGearSlotWorn? = null,
    /** The band's best-in-slot pick for the spec and the character's faction (from the export's race, else the faction the Battle.net import stored), as the Forever Sixty Data addon ships it: the leveling-bis ladder's pick for the band without raid buffs, except that an item whose stats the client has not confirmed is never a pick. Every slot whose own pick is confirmed keeps it; each other slot takes the next confirmed candidate in the ladder's order that the band's rules allow beside them: the two slots of a pair (the rings, the trinkets, the two hands) never hold the same item (the same id or the same name), and there is no off-hand pick beside a two-handed main-hand pick. Null when the band has no pick for the slot, the character has no rated spec or is below level 20, or its faction or the spec's best-in-slot data is unknown. */
    @SerialName("pick") val pick: CharacterGearSlotPick? = null,
    /** The Gear component points the pick would add over the worn item, one decimal: 500 x (the pick's gear score - the worn item's gear score) / the band's best set's gear score, each item scored by the spec's stat weights as the Gear component scores it. An empty slot scores 0. 0 when the worn item is the pick or scores at least as much; an upgrade worth under 0.05 points also rounds to 0. The rings and the trinkets are matched to their picks whichever way round gives the smaller total, so a pick worn in the other slot of its pair reads 0. When the picked or the worn main hand is two-handed, the two hands count as one unit: the main hand's gap is the picked main and off hands' score less the worn main and off hands' score (0 at least), and the off hand's gap is 0, or null when the band has no off-hand pick. Null when there is no pick, when an item is not in the data build, or when the band's best set cannot be scored. */
    @SerialName("gap") val gap: Double? = null,
)

/** The band's best-in-slot pick for the spec and the character's faction (from the export's race, else the faction the Battle.net import stored), as the Forever Sixty Data addon ships it: the leveling-bis ladder's pick for the band without raid buffs, except that an item whose stats the client has not confirmed is never a pick. Every slot whose own pick is confirmed keeps it; each other slot takes the next confirmed candidate in the ladder's order that the band's rules allow beside them: the two slots of a pair (the rings, the trinkets, the two hands) never hold the same item (the same id or the same name), and there is no off-hand pick beside a two-handed main-hand pick. Null when the band has no pick for the slot, the character has no rated spec or is below level 20, or its faction or the spec's best-in-slot data is unknown. */
@Serializable
data class CharacterGearSlotPick(
    @SerialName("id") val id: Int,
    @SerialName("name") val name: String,
    /** Where the item comes from, as a player knows it: "Wailing Caverns: Mutanus the Devourer", "Blacksmithing", "The League of Arathor". */
    @SerialName("source") val source: String,
    /** The drop chance as a fraction (0.333333 is one in three), at the pick's own source; a pick promoted past an item the client has not confirmed carries the chance of its own source. Null when the source states no rate (every quest, vendor, crafted, reputation and PvP source, and a drop whose loot table gives none). */
    @SerialName("chance") val chance: Double? = null,
)

